<?xml version='1.0' encoding='UTF-8'?>
<map xmlns="http://openorienteering.org/apps/mapper/xml/v2" version="9">
    <notes>INFO (course setter to include on map)
Title:
	North of firebreak: Woodend Beach
	South of firebreak: Kairaki Beach
Scale: 1:15,000
Contour interval: 2.5m
North lines: 300m apart


CREDITS (course setter to include on map - 6pt Arial)
Cartography:
	1. Woodend Beach North towards Pegasus: C. Jørgensen 2016
	2. Woodend Beach South to Firebreak: M. Croxford 2019, Updates: R. Moore 2023
	3. Firebreak to Kairaki Beach: R. Higham 2020
	4. Inland paddocks: C. Jørgensen 2021
Copyright © Peninsula and Plains Orienteers
Possession of this map does not imply right of access
Non-commercial use only unless otherwise granted
Map version: d3f9a5a


COORDINATORS' NOTES (map coordinator to update + commit on map being sent)
Last sent to: Briana Steven &lt;briana.banana888@gmail.com&gt;


CONTROLLERS' NOTES (controller to read upon map being sent)
Vegetation in big flat area should not be relied on for control features
All courses may need to be approved 2-3 weeks before event with Landowners (see permissions).
Hazards include traffic, mountain bikers, pedestrians, sea, prickly bushes, windfall, horses.


MAPPERS' NOTES
Residential areas have only been shown as OOB where there is a dwelling, otherwise open - unsure of the title status.
Single rope fences are not shown.
Completely recreated from 2014 Lidar by Russell Higham during June 2020
HAZARD: The big flat area has much dead vegetation including large trees.This presents a trip hazard in long grass, and overhead from from large falling branches - mapped as fight.</notes>
